 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Reproduction is the making of new individuals of the same kind by living things. Without it a species would die out when its members die.\nThere are two kinds:\n• Asexual reproduction: one parent, no sex cells. The offspring are identical to the parent (a clone). Examples: a banana sucker, an onion bulb, a cassava stem cutting.\n• Sexual reproduction: two sex cells (gametes), a male and a female, join (fertilisation). The offspring are similar to the parents but not identical: there is variation. In flowering plants the flower is the organ of sexual reproduction, and it produces seeds.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "p": "plantain"
  },
  "problem": "A farmer plants suckers from his best {p} tree. Is this sexual or asexual reproduction? What will the new plants be like?",
  "steps": [
   "A sucker grows from one parent plant, with no sex cells: this is asexual reproduction.",
   "The new plants are clones: identical to the parent, so they keep its good qualities."
  ],
  "answer": "Asexual reproduction; the new plants are identical to the parent.",
  "checks": []
 },
